# TD IT Solution Insurance — Asset Protection & Recovery Platform

Enterprise InsurTech platform: customers subscribe to monthly plans and register valuable
assets (vehicles, laptops, phones, tablets, TVs, desktops, business equipment). Registered
assets can carry GPS tracking hardware; the platform ingests location data to help locate
and recover lost/stolen assets, coordinating with security-company partners.

## Current repo state — verify before assuming anything

This repo has moved well past a design-system showcase. As of this handoff (verify against
`HANDOFF.md`, which moves faster than this file):
- **Web** (`src/`): React 18 + Vite + TS + Tailwind design-system components, marketing site,
  **plus** real product surfaces — Admin Panel (`/admin/*`), Security Company Dashboard
  (`/security/*`), and a full customer surface (auth, onboarding wizard, post-login dashboard).
- **Backend** (`backend/`): real Node.js + TS API — Feature 001 (auth), Feature 004 customer
  **and admin** policies/assets routes, a recovery-case API scaffold, and Feature 006/007
  (onboarding/plan-catalog, notifications) are built and tested (**188 tests green, 36 files** —
  re-verify with `cd backend && npm test`, this number moves every session). Claims and payments
  are **not built**.
- **Mobile** (`mobile/`): real Expo + TS app — auth, Policy/Assets tabs, a full onboarding
  wizard, and a notification-preferences screen wired to live API; Phase 2 recovery/claims **UI
  scaffold** (stub APIs, backend 404s). **12 test files** (re-verify pass count with
  `cd mobile && npm test`). App icon/splash are the real brand mark, not Expo defaults.
- **Databases**: MongoDB Atlas (domain data) + Supabase Postgres (identity/session data), per
  ADR-0002's polyglot split. Both have real, applied schemas.
- **Feature 008** (self-device GPS tracking): design-time only, four documents under
  `docs/features/008-self-device-gps-tracking/` plus ADR-0009. **Nothing implemented.** Don't
  add `expo-location` or any location code on the strength of the design docs alone.

Read `HANDOFF.md` at repo root before starting any new work — it has the full current-state
snapshot, open items, and what's mid-flight. Don't re-derive from git log alone.

## Non-negotiable rules

- **Never claim a system/integration/feature exists if it hasn't been built** — this repo has
  a documented history of catching exactly this kind of false claim. Check before asserting.
- **No secrets/credentials in source.** `.env.local` (repo root) and `mobile/.env` hold real
  local dev credentials — both gitignored, never commit them, never paste secret values into
  chat/rules/docs. See `docs/features/001-authentication/secrets-management-plan.md`.
- **New UI components reuse `src/components/*` first**; new one-off components need
  `design-system-manager` standards sign-off (see role index below) even without that role
  literally reviewing — apply its documented conventions.
- **Every non-trivial feature passes through the 15-stage lifecycle** in
  `docs/organization/02-feature-lifecycle.md`. Stage 8 (Security Review) and Stage 10 (QA
  Testing) are hard gates — never skipped for speed, even under time pressure.
- **Architecture-significant decisions become ADRs** under `docs/organization/adr/`, following
  ADR-0001 through ADR-0006 as precedent for format and rigor. Check existing ADRs before
  reopening a settled decision — but do reopen one if a named revisit trigger fires.
- **Compliance framework is POPIA** (South Africa) — see
  `docs/features/001-authentication/compliance-review-supabase.md` for the governing analysis
  on cross-border data flows, retention, and third-party operators. Any new third-party
  service touching PII needs the same s72/DPA/RoPA treatment before going live, not after.

## Stack baseline (ADR-0001, refined by ADR-0002)

- Web: React/Vite/TS/Tailwind (existing).
- Mobile: Expo (React Native) + TypeScript.
- Backend: Node.js + TypeScript, `/api/v1` prefix, cursor-based pagination, uniform error
  envelope `{ error: { code, message, requestId } }` — see `api-design.md` files for the
  ratified contract, don't invent a parallel convention.
- **Identity/session data → Supabase** (Postgres + Supabase Auth). **Everything else
  (policies, assets, GPS/location history, claims) → MongoDB.** The backend is the *only*
  layer permitted to talk to either store directly — no client (mobile, admin dashboard)
  ever holds a Supabase or MongoDB credential.
- Payment gateway and GPS hardware vendor remain open decisions (`integration-architect`
  territory) — don't hardcode an assumed vendor.

## Role index

This project's governance model (`docs/organization/`) defines 35 specialized roles, each
with a detailed spec at `.claude/agents/<role-name>.md` (mission, responsibilities, standards).
Those files were written for a different tool's subagent-spawning system, but the
**standards and conventions inside them are still the source of truth** — read the relevant
file(s) below before doing non-trivial work in that domain, the same way you'd read a style
guide.

| Domain | Roles (file: `.claude/agents/<name>.md`) |
|---|---|
| Cross-cutting / strategy | `cto`, `solution-architect`\*, `product-manager`, `technical-project-manager` |
| Backend | `backend-architect`, `backend-engineer`, `authentication-engineer` |
| Database | `database-architect` |
| Mobile | `mobile-architect`, `mobile-engineer` |
| Web frontend | `frontend-architect`, `frontend-engineer`, `design-system-manager`, `ui-designer` |
| Security | `cybersecurity-architect`, `security-engineer` |
| Compliance | `compliance-specialist` |
| Integrations/vendors | `integration-architect`, `gps-integration-engineer`, `payment-engineer`, `notification-engineer` |
| Infra/ops | `cloud-infrastructure-architect`, `devops-engineer`, `site-reliability-engineer`, `performance-engineer` |
| QA | `qa-architect`, `automation-qa-engineer`, `manual-qa-engineer` |
| Data/analytics | `analytics-specialist`, `reporting-engineer`, `ai-solutions-architect`, `recommendation-engine-specialist` |
| Research/product | `ux-researcher`, `business-analyst` |
| Docs | `technical-writer` |

\* `solution-architect` is referenced by the governance docs (chairs Architecture Review,
co-ratifies ADRs) but has no corresponding file in `.claude/agents/` — treat `cto` as the
fallback owner for that stage until/unless the org docs are updated.

Domain-specific rules in this `.cursor/rules/` directory attach the relevant subset of these
automatically based on file path; this table is for anything that falls outside those globs.
